## What This Project Taught Me

One of the biggest things this project reinforced for me is that **AI engineering is not simply about putting an LLM into an application**.

The interesting engineering problems begin after the model exists.

How does it obtain reliable information?

How does it interact with external systems?

How are its capabilities constrained?

How are its outputs validated?

How do multiple agents coordinate?

How do you handle conflicting recommendations?

How do you deal with failures?

How do you evaluate whether an agent made the correct decision?

How do you preserve observability?

How do you prevent an intelligent system from having more authority than it should?

These questions pushed the project beyond the level of a simple AI demonstration.

It became an exploration of how AI can participate in a larger cloud engineering system.

