## The Broader Engineering Philosophy

The underlying philosophy of the project can be summarised quite simply:

> **AI should increase engineering capability, not remove engineering discipline.**

The objective is not to create an AI that blindly changes infrastructure.

It is to create an AI system that can help engineers understand complex environments, identify opportunities, explore alternatives, evaluate trade-offs and make better-informed decisions.

That distinction is important to me.

I am interested in the point where AI moves beyond generating text and becomes part of a real engineering workflow.

That means giving agents access to meaningful tools and information, but also giving them boundaries.

It means allowing automation where automation makes sense, while retaining human judgement where the consequences of an action justify it.

It means using AI to accelerate analysis without pretending that an LLM can replace architectural responsibility.

